  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">20 Anniversary Guatemalan Peace Accords - 20 Anniversary Guatemalan Peace Accords Propaz</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">20 Anniversary Guatemalan Peace Accords</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consensus is reached among different Guatemalan sectors, about the relevance of the 1996 Peace Accords, as an agenda for inclusive and democratic development, addressing the challenges of strengthening of the Guatemalan democracy, with the purpose of creating support of relevant stakeholders for the implementation of pending issues and reforms included in the Peace Accords in the areas of Human Rights and Justice, Gender, Indigenous Peoples, Agrarian situation and Public Security.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Fredsavtalen som  undertecknades f&#xf6;r 20 &#xe5;r sedan har endast delvis genomf&#xf6;rts och utg&#xf6;r fortsatt en mycket viktig utg&#xe5;ngspunkt f&#xf6;r utvecklingspolitiken i ett land pr&#xe4;glat av djupa sociala klyftor och konflikter. Insatsen syftar till &#xf6;ka f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;elsen och v&#xe4;cka debatt kring Fredsavtalen som en relevant utvecklingsagenda f&#xf6;r Guatemala, och d&#xe4;rmed stimulera till reformer f&#xf6;r dess fulla genomf&#xf6;rande. Insatsen innefattar st&#xf6;d till fyra guatemalanska civilsamh&#xe4;llsorganisationer med h&#xf6;g trov&#xe4;rdighet. Organisationerna kommer att genomf&#xf6;ra analys samt ordna seminarium och andra aktiviteter f&#xf6;r att uppm&#xe4;rksamma Fredsavtalens betydelse.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention targets the 20 anniversary of the Peace Accords, as an opportunity to address the pending issues of the peace process for the building of a strong democratic institutions, which facilitates the protection of human rights, the economical development, and the inclusion of indigenous peoples, among other aspects. The counterparts of this program, four Guatemalan civil society organizations ( Fundacion Propaz, Demos, Fundaci&#xf3;n Esquipulas and Fundamaya) will conduct research, analysis, advocacy and organize public debates to promote an informed discussion on the Peace Accords and raise awareness about the importance of addressing the pending issues of those Peace Accords.</narrative>
  </description>
